+# genkit-app
+
+A Genkit Python app. Entrypoint: `src/main.py`.
+
+## Before writing Genkit code
+
+Load the `developing-genkit-python` skill (or read its references under
+`~/.claude/skills/developing-genkit-python/references/`) before writing or
+debugging any Genkit code. It covers setup, agents, flows, tools, streaming,
+FastAPI serving, dotprompt, evals, and common errors in detail.
+
+## Rules
+
+- **Agent or flow?** Conversational / multi-turn / "assistant"-like features
+  use `ai.define_agent` (see `references/agents.md`). Single-shot, stateless
+  generation uses a plain `@ai.flow()`.
+- **Imports are public only**: `genkit`, `genkit_google_genai`, `genkit_fastapi`,
+  `genkit_middleware`, `genkit_evaluators`, `genkit.agent`, `genkit.embedder`,
+  `genkit.evaluator`, `genkit.model`. Never import internal modules
+  (`genkit._core`, ...).
+- **Entry via `ai.run_main(main())`** — required for `genkit start` to capture
+  traces correctly.
+- **Model ids are prefixed**, e.g. `googleai/gemini-flash-latest`.
+- **Tool parameters must be a Pydantic `BaseModel`** (bare scalars get a 400
+  from Gemini). Define tools with `@ai.tool()`, not `@ai.define_tool()`.
+- **`GEMINI_API_KEY`** must be set in the environment before running.
+- Use **`uv`** for all dependency management (`uv add genkit-<plugin>`, `uv
+  sync`, `uv run`). Never install into the system interpreter.
+
+## Running and verifying changes
+
+Don't just `uv run src/main.py` — it skips trace capture, so you're debugging
+blind. Use the Genkit CLI instead:
+
+```bash
+# Non-interactive, one-shot check of a flow (prints a Trace ID, then exits):
+genkit flow:run tell_joke '{"topic": "Python"}' --non-interactive -- uv run src/main.py
+
+# Inspect what actually happened (model I/O, tool calls, errors):
+genkit trace:list
+genkit trace:get <traceId> --format json
+```
+
+`genkit start -- uv run src/main.py` runs a persistent dev server + Dev UI —
+useful for interactive sessions, but it blocks until Ctrl+C, so don't use it
+as a blocking step in automated checks.
+
+See `references/dev-workflow.md` and `references/common-errors.md` in the
+skill for the full checklist.
